  "scenario": "A continuous catalytic reactor unit running a fixed-bed hydrogenation has seen reactor conversion fall about 20% over the past month, staying low run after run. The decline followed a switch to a new feedstock supplier after a routine catalyst reload. The process team's leading theories are that the reactor is running too cool or at the wrong pressure, so they favor retuning temperature and pressure. Effluent analysis has shown a slightly elevated byproduct fraction. Routine unit data read broadly within range. The feed, temperature, purification, and regeneration systems are all adjustable, and polishing and regeneration options are available. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available controls or treatments, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the loss and what to do about it.",
